Wire the NPU MMU to the mainline rockchip-iommu driver.

One node covering both cores' bank pairs (registers from the vendor
tree: core_base + 0x2000/0x2100), using the rk3568-iommu compatible
the other rk3576 MMUs use upstream. The mainline driver supports one
IOMMU instance per master - a per-core split leaves the second
instance unlinked and its core in bypass (jobs then time out with no
page faults, reading unmapped IOVAs as physical addresses).

With iommus present the rknpu driver leaves CMA/contiguous mode:
buffers become pageable and the 256 MB CMA cap no longer applies to
the NPU.

Signed-off-by: Isaiah Peng <isaiahdw@gmail.com>

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3576-armsom-sige5.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3576-armsom-sige5.dts
@@ -1073,8 +1073,35 @@
 		power-domains = <&power RK3576_PD_NPU0>,
 				<&power RK3576_PD_NPU1>;
 		power-domain-names = "npu0", "npu1";
+		iommus = <&rknpu_mmu>;
 		status = "okay";
 	};
+
+	/*
+	 * NPU MMU, driven by the mainline rockchip-iommu driver (the same
+	 * v2 IP the rk3576 video-decoder MMU uses upstream). One node
+	 * covering both cores' bank pairs (core_base + 0x2000/0x2100),
+	 * mirroring the vendor tree: the mainline driver supports one
+	 * IOMMU instance per master, so per-core nodes leave one core's
+	 * MMU unlinked and in bypass. The node holds NPU0's power domain;
+	 * NPU1 is held by the NPU driver whenever the MMU is touched.
+	 */
+	rknpu_mmu: iommu@27702000 {
+		compatible = "rockchip,rk3576-iommu", "rockchip,rk3568-iommu";
+		reg = <0x0 0x27702000 0x0 0x100>,
+		      <0x0 0x27702100 0x0 0x100>,
+		      <0x0 0x2770a000 0x0 0x100>,
+		      <0x0 0x2770a100 0x0 0x100>;
+		interrupts = <GIC_SPI 247 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>,
+			     <GIC_SPI 248 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
+		clocks = <&cru ACLK_RKNN0>, <&cru ACLK_RKNN1>,
+			 <&cru HCLK_RKNN_ROOT>, <&cru ACLK_RKNN_CBUF>,
+			 <&cru HCLK_RKNN_CBUF>;
+		clock-names = "aclk0", "aclk1", "iface",
+			      "aclk_cbuf", "hclk_cbuf";
+		#iommu-cells = <0>;
+		power-domains = <&power RK3576_PD_NPU0>;
+	};
 };
 
